  "readmeFile": "Package.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixed: RateLimitWindow.ResetsAt (and other string-typed timestamp fields parsed off the CLI's control-response JSON) could come back reformatted as a locale-specific date string (e.g. \"07/27/2026 08:20:00\") instead of the CLI's original ISO-8601 text, with the UTC \"Z\" designator silently dropped. ClaudeCodeTransport parsed each stdout line with JObject.Parse's default DateParseHandling, which auto-converts ISO-8601-looking JSON strings into DateTime tokens while building the JObject tree; when that DateTime was later coerced into a string-typed property, Json.NET rendered it via CultureInfo.InvariantCulture instead of preserving the source text. Stdout lines are now parsed with DateParseHandling.None so date-like strings pass through unmodified.",
